{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Model-View Update Order.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Model-View Update Order.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender model view update order blender model view update order","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Model-View Update Order.md","fileName":"Blender Model-View Update Order.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Model-View Update Order","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:20\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Core Source Architecture]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Core Source Architecture","Blender Main Event Loop","Blender Event Distribution Pipeline","Blender Editor Draw Pipeline","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Model-View Update Order.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Model-View Update Order.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender model view update order blender model view update order","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Model-View Update Order.md","fileName":"Blender Model-View Update Order.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Model-View Update Order","heading":"Blender Model-View Update Order","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Blender's main loop updates application data before it redraws the interface. Events and operator callbacks first change the model; notifiers record consequences; only after those steps does the draw update refresh what the user sees.\n\nThis sequence reflects a model-view-controller organization and prevents the view from presenting an intermediate state. The ordering joins the [[Blender Main Event Loop]] to both the [[Blender Event Distribution Pipeline]] and the [[Blender Editor Draw Pipeline]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Core Source Architecture","Blen